solutions.latex:
Choose a class at random (probability $\dfrac12$ each), then a girl from it. 7C has 30 pupils, 12 girls, so $P=\dfrac25$. 7K has 28 pupils, 16 girls, so $P=\dfrac47$.

\exfigure{1325_q18_s1}
$$\begin{aligned} P(\text{girl})&=\dfrac12\times\dfrac25+\dfrac12\times\dfrac47 \\ &=\dfrac15+\dfrac27 \\ &=\dfrac{17}{35} \end{aligned}$$

\exfigure{1328_q27_s1}

Each coin is chosen with probability $\dfrac{1}{3}$. Add the two ways of getting a tail: the fake coin, or a fair coin.
$$\begin{aligned} P(T) &= \dfrac{1}{3}\times 1 + \dfrac{2}{3}\times\dfrac{1}{2} \\ &= \dfrac{2}{3} \end{aligned}$$

